---
import Full from '../layouts/Full.astro';
import octicons from '@primer/octicons';
// Rendered by the CLI itself and converted to spans, not drawn by hand. See
// README: a chart nobody could draw convincingly is the one worth not faking.
import monitor from '../monitor.inc.html?raw';

const repo = 'https://github.com/nicodes/komizo';
const docs = 'https://github.com/nicodes/komizo-be';
const actions = 'https://github.com/nicodes/komizo-actions';
const icon = (name: keyof typeof octicons, size = 16) =>
	octicons[name].toSVG({ width: size, height: size });
---

<Full
	title="komizo — Devops for your health"
	description="Devops for your health. CI never writes to your box: one tag crosses SSH and root does the rest. One Caddy for HTTPS, and a terminal interface that shows what every app is serving and spending."
>
	<div class="page-shell">
		<header class="site-header">
			<a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="komizo home">
				<svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true">
					<path d="M16 3 28 10v12L16 29 4 22V10L16 3Z"></path>
					<path d="M12 12v8M12 16l7-4M12 16l7 4"></path>
				</svg>
				<span>komizo</span>
			</a>
			<a class="header-cta" href={repo}>GitHub <span class="icon" set:html={icon('arrow-up-right', 14)} /></a>
		</header>

		<main>
			<section class="hero">
				<div class="hero-copy">
					<p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Your server. Your keys.</p>
					<h1>Devops for your <em>health.</em></h1>
					<p class="lede">
						CI builds an image and sends one string over SSH. Root on your box pulls it, writes
						the compose file and brings the stack up. No agent, no dashboard, and nobody else
						holding your production.
					</p>
					<div class="hero-actions">
						<code class="install">go install github.com/nicodes/komizo@latest</code>
						<p>MIT · Alpine hosts · one static binary</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="product-frame" aria-label="the komizo interface">
					<div class="frame-bar">
						<div class="frame-brand"><span class="menu-lines"></span> komizo / box.example.com</div>
						<div class="frame-actions"><span class="icon" set:html={icon('server', 13)} /><span class="icon" set:html={icon('pulse', 13)} /></div>
					</div>
					<div class="tui">
						<pre><span class="k">os</span>             alpine
<span class="k">proxy</span>          <span class="ok">●</span> running
<span class="k">network</span>        <span class="ok">●</span> edge  bridge
<span class="k">komizo</span>         94d5dbd1333d
<span class="k">docker</span>         Docker version 26.1.3
<span class="k">processor</span>      <span class="bar-ok">████</span><span class="bar-off">████████████████</span>  18%   4 cores
<span class="k">memory</span>         <span class="bar-ok">██████████</span><span class="bar-off">██████████</span>  49%   1.9G of 3.9G
<span class="k">disk</span>           <span class="bar-warn">█████████████████</span><span class="bar-off">███</span>  84%   32G of 39G

<span class="cur">▍</span> <span class="ok">●</span>  blog          a1b2c3d4e5f6  <span class="spark">▆▇▇▇█▆▇▇██▇▇▇█▆▇</span>          <span class="err">▃▇█</span>       ghcr.io/you/blog-config
  <span class="ok">●</span>  ├ gateway     :80           <span class="spark">▆█▇▇█▇▇█▇▇█▇▇█▇▇</span>                    blog.example.com
  <span class="ok">●</span>  ├ api         :8080         <span class="spark">▆▆▇▇█▆▆▇██▇▇▇█▆▆</span>          <span class="err">▃▇█</span>       api.blog.example.com
  <span class="ok">●</span>  └ db          :5432         <span class="dots">················</span>  <span class="dots">················</span>  pb.blog.example.com

  <span class="ok">●</span>  shop          9f04354ac1de  <span class="spark">▃▃▄▄▃▃▄▅▄▄▃▃▄▄▅▄</span>                    ghcr.io/you/shop-config</pre>
					</div>
					<div class="frame-keys"><span>enter</span> monitor<i></i><span>s</span> stop<i></i><span>l</span> logs<i></i><span>q</span> quit</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="principles" aria-label="How komizo works">
				<article>
					<span class="number">01</span>
					<div>
						<h2>CI cannot write to your server</h2>
						<p>
							The deploy artefact is a config image. One tag crosses the SSH connection and root
							on your box pulls it. A stolen CI token can deploy a tag and set a secret — it cannot
							read one back, run a container, or get a shell.
						</p>
					</div>
				</article>
				<article>
					<span class="number">02</span>
					<div>
						<h2>Apps cannot reach each other</h2>
						<p>
							One Caddy terminates TLS and hands each hostname to the app that claimed it. Every
							app fronts itself with its own gateway, so nothing shared holds an app's config —
							and two apps can both have a container called <code>api</code>.
						</p>
					</div>
				</article>
				<article>
					<span class="number">03</span>
					<div>
						<h2>Nothing on the screen is invented</h2>
						<p>
							Requests come off the proxy's own access log; processor, memory and disk off
							<code>/proc</code> and the cgroups. Every value is a measurement or a gap — a
							container nobody sampled reads as unknown, never as zero.
						</p>
					</div>
				</article>
			</section>

			<section class="monitor-section" aria-label="the monitor">
				<div class="section-head">
					<p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Press enter</p>
					<h2>Then find out what it did.</h2>
					<p>
						Requests and failures come off the shared proxy's access log, attributed to the app
						by hostname — nothing is asked of the app. Processor, memory and disk come off
						<code>/proc</code> and the cgroups, written down once a minute so there is a
						yesterday to look at.
					</p>
					<p class="aside">
						The line laid over each chart is how unusual that minute was, against a trailing
						median of the half hour before it. Green within one deviation, amber to two, red
						past it — and nothing at all where there is no baseline yet, because "we cannot say"
						and "exactly normal" must not share a shape.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="product-frame wide">
					<div class="frame-bar">
						<div class="frame-brand"><span class="menu-lines"></span> komizo / box.example.com / blog / api / monitor</div>
						<div class="frame-actions"><span class="icon" set:html={icon('graph', 13)} /><span class="icon" set:html={icon('clock', 13)} /></div>
					</div>
					<div class="tui monitor"><pre set:html={monitor} /></div>
					<div class="frame-keys"><span>t</span> range<i></i><span>r</span> refresh<i></i><span>esc</span> back<i></i><span>q</span> quit</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="closing">
				<p>Merge.<br />It's live.</p>
				<div><span>GITHUB ACTIONS</span><i></i><span>YOUR REGISTRY</span><i></i><span>YOUR SERVER</span></div>
				<div class="closing-actions">
					<a class="primary-cta light" href={repo}>Get the CLI <span class="icon" set:html={icon('arrow-right', 16)} /></a>
					<a class="ghost-cta" href={docs}>Read the docs <span class="icon" set:html={icon('arrow-up-right', 14)} /></a>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>

		<footer>
			<a class="brand footer-brand" href="/"><span>komizo</span></a>
			<p><a href={repo}>cli</a> · <a href={actions}>actions</a> · <a href={docs}>docs</a></p>
			<p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} komizo</p>
		</footer>
	</div>
</Full>

<style>
	.page-shell { min-height: 100svh; overflow-x: hidden; }
	.site-header { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px)); height: 76px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; }
	.brand { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; color: var(--ink); font-size: 19px; font-weight: 760; letter-spacing: -.03em; text-decoration: none; }
	.brand-mark { width: 27px; height: 27px; }
	.brand-mark path:first-child { fill: var(--ink); stroke: none; }
	.brand-mark path:last-child { fill: none; stroke: var(--cyan); stroke-width: 2; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
	.header-cta { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; color: var(--ink); border-bottom: 1px solid #c3c8c8; padding: 6px 0; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 650; text-decoration: none; white-space: nowrap; }
	.header-cta span { margin-left: 5px; color: var(--cyan-dark); }
	:global(.icon svg) { display: block; fill: currentColor; }

	.hero { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px)); margin: 70px auto 110px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: .85fr 1.15fr; align-items: center; gap: 70px; }
	.hero-copy { position: relative; z-index: 2; }
	.eyebrow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; margin: 0 0 22px; color: var(--quiet); font: 620 11px/1 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
	.eyebrow span { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--cyan-dark); box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(11, 114, 133, .12); }
	h1 { max-width: 600px; margin: 0; color: var(--ink); font-size: clamp(46px, 6vw, 78px); font-weight: 590; line-height: .98; letter-spacing: -.062em; }
	h1 em { color: var(--cyan-dark); font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400; }
	.lede { max-width: 520px; margin: 30px 0 32px; color: var(--quiet); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; }
	.hero-actions { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 14px; }
	.install { display: block; max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid #d3d8d8; border-radius: 5px; background: white; padding: 13px 16px; color: var(--ink); font: 500 12.5px/1 var(--mono); white-space: nowrap; }
	.hero-actions p { margin: 0; color: #868f8f; font: 500 10px/1.4 var(--mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; }

	/* The interface, as it renders. Text rather than a screenshot: it stays
	   selectable, it scales with the reader's font, and it cannot go blurry on
	   a display the screenshot was not taken for. */
	.product-frame { position: relative; min-width: 680px; border: 1px solid #d3d8d8; border-radius: 9px; background: white; box-shadow: 0 35px 80px rgba(18, 40, 45, .13), 0 3px 10px rgba(18, 40, 45, .07); overflow: hidden; transform: perspective(1400px) rotateY(-3deg) rotateX(1deg); }
	.product-frame::before { content: ''; position: absolute; z-index: -1; width: 340px; height: 340px; right: -70px; top: -90px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--cyan); filter: blur(80px); opacity: .3; }
	.frame-bar { height: 42px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; border-bottom: 1px solid #e6eaea; padding: 0 13px; color: #525c5e; font: 600 10px var(--mono); }
	.frame-brand, .frame-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 11px; }
	.menu-lines { width: 13px; height: 8px; border-block: 1px solid #757e80; position: relative; }
	.menu-lines::after { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 3px; border-top: 1px solid #757e80; }
	.frame-actions span { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 22px; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px; background: #f0f3f3; color: #424a4b; }
	.tui { background: #0b0f10; padding: 18px 20px; overflow-x: auto; }
	.tui pre { margin: 0; color: #d6dcdc; font: 11.5px/1.75 var(--mono); }
	.tui .k { color: #7a8486; }
	.tui .ok { color: #69db7c; }
	.tui .err { color: #ff6b6b; }
	.tui .spark { color: #3bc9db; }
	.tui .dots { color: #4a5254; }
	.tui .bar-ok { color: #69db7c; }
	.tui .bar-warn { color: #ffd43b; }
	.tui .bar-off { color: #2c3335; }
	.tui .cur { color: var(--cyan); }
	.frame-keys { height: 34px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; border-top: 1px solid #1b2122; background: #0b0f10; padding: 0 20px; color: #6d7678; font: 9.5px var(--mono); }
	.frame-keys span { color: var(--cyan); font-weight: 500; }
	.frame-keys i { width: 3px; height: 3px; border-radius: 50%; background: #333c3d; }

	.principles { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px)); margin: 0 auto 120px; border-top: 1px solid #d5dada; }
	.principles article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr; border-bottom: 1px solid #d5dada; padding: 32px 0; }
	.principles article div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .75fr 1fr; align-items: baseline; gap: 40px; }
	.number { color: var(--cyan-dark); font: 650 10px var(--mono); }
	.principles h2 { margin: 0; color: var(--ink); font-size: 22px; font-weight: 580; letter-spacing: -.035em; }
	.principles p { max-width: 560px; margin: 0; color: var(--quiet); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }
	.principles code { border-radius: 3px; background: #e4e8e8; padding: 1px 5px; font: 12px var(--mono); }

	.monitor-section { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px)); margin: 0 auto 110px; }
	.section-head { max-width: 620px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
	.section-head h2 { margin: 0 0 22px; color: var(--ink); font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 46px); font-weight: 560; line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
	.section-head p { margin: 0 0 14px; color: var(--quiet); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; }
	.section-head .aside { max-width: 580px; color: #7b8486; font-size: 13.5px; }
	.section-head code { border-radius: 3px; background: #e4e8e8; padding: 1px 5px; font: 12px var(--mono); }
	.product-frame.wide { min-width: 0; width: 100%; max-width: 100%; transform: none; }
	.tui.monitor { padding: 20px 22px; }
	/* The chart is 108 columns and does not reflow -- it is a rendering of a
	   terminal, and rewrapping it would be a rendering of nothing. So it scrolls
	   INSIDE its own frame at any width, and the page never grows to fit it. */
	.tui.monitor pre { width: max-content; font-size: 10px; line-height: 1.6; }

	.closing { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px)); margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 8px; background: var(--ink); color: white; padding: 65px; }
	.closing > p { max-width: 680px; margin: 0 0 50px; font-size: clamp(42px, 6vw, 72px); font-weight: 530; line-height: .98; letter-spacing: -.055em; }
	.closing > div { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 13px; margin-bottom: 35px; color: #99a2a3; font: 560 9px var(--mono); letter-spacing: .09em; }
	.closing > div i { width: 50px; border-top: 1px dashed #545c5d; }
	.closing-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 22px; }
	.closing-actions i { display: none; }
	.primary-cta { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 30px; border-radius: 4px; background: var(--ink); color: white; padding: 14px 18px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 680; text-decoration: none; transition: transform .18s ease, background .18s ease; }
	.primary-cta:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }
	.primary-cta.light { background: var(--cyan); color: #0a1a1d; }
	.primary-cta.light span { color: #0a1a1d; }
	.ghost-cta { color: #c8d0d1; border-bottom: 1px solid #3a4344; padding: 6px 0; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 650; text-decoration: none; }
	.ghost-cta span { margin-left: 5px; color: var(--cyan); }

	footer { width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 40px)); min-height: 120px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; align-items: center; color: #868f8f; font: 500 10px var(--mono); }
	footer p:nth-child(2) { text-align: center; }
	footer p:last-child { text-align: right; }
	footer a { color: #868f8f; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccd2d2; }
	footer a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
	.footer-brand { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16px; border: 0; }

	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		.hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; margin-top: 45px; gap: 60px; }
		.hero-copy { max-width: 680px; }
		.product-frame { min-width: 0; width: 100%; transform: none; }
		.principles article div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 9px; }
	}
	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.site-header, .hero, .principles, .closing, footer { width: min(100% - 28px, 1180px); }
		.site-header { height: 64px; }
		.hero { margin: 48px auto 80px; }
		.eyebrow { margin-bottom: 18px; }
		h1 { font-size: clamp(42px, 13vw, 60px); }
		.lede { margin-top: 24px; font-size: 15px; }
		.install { font-size: 11px; padding: 11px 13px; }
		.product-frame { border-radius: 6px; }
		.tui { padding: 14px; }
		.tui pre { font-size: 9px; line-height: 1.7; }
		.tui.monitor { padding: 12px 14px; }
		.tui.monitor pre { font-size: 7.5px; line-height: 1.55; }
		.section-head { margin-bottom: 28px; }
		.principles article { grid-template-columns: 42px 1fr; padding: 26px 0; }
		.principles h2 { font-size: 19px; }
		.principles p { font-size: 13px; }
		.closing { padding: 40px 25px; }
		.closing > div { flex-wrap: wrap; }
		.closing > div i { width: 20px; }
		.closing-actions { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 16px; }
		footer { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; padding: 30px 0; }
		.footer-brand { display: none; }
		footer p:nth-child(2) { text-align: left; }
	}
</style>
